  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Zooplankton Biomass Data Around Japan",
  "description": "A collection of zooplankton biomass data (wet mass) compiled by Kazuko Odate, sampled from 1951 - 1990 around Japan (Northwest Pacific) available through COPEPOD. See the cruise summary web page for a detailed list of cruise dates, number of tows and sampled data. Data can be directly downloaded from the COPEPOD website. Coastal & Oceanic Plankton Ecology, Production & Observation Database (COPEPOD) is an on-line global plankton database by NOAA - National Marine Fisheries Service (NMFS). Dataset of Zooplankton Biomass in the Western North Pacific Ocean (1951-1990, K. Odate Collection). This compilation was an effort of the Tohoku National Fisheries Research Institute (TNFRI), the Japan Oceanographic Data Center (JODC), and the Marine Information Research Center (MIRC). [Reference: Kazuko Odate 1991: Distribution of Zooplankton Biomass in the Northwestern Pacific Ocean, 1951-1988: Mean Wet Weight of Collections by Year, Month and 1-degree Squares. Tohoku National Fisheries Research Institute, Japan, 370 pp.] [Reference: Kazuko Odate 1994: Zooplankton Biomass and its Long-Term Variation in the Western North Pacific Ocean, Tohoku Sea Area, JAPAN. The Bulletin of Tohoku National Fisheries Research Institute, No.56, 115-173.]\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To provide investigators with an integrated data set of quality-controlled, globally distributed plankton abundance, biomass and composition data, along with co-sampled environmental data.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23568456",
